# Constants

Put tunable numbers and strings in the `constants.ts` of the domain that owns them (`src/ship/constants.ts`, `src/abduction/constants.ts`, `src/camera/constants.ts`, `src/player/constants.ts`, `src/ui/constants.ts`). There is no top-level `src/constants.ts`. A new domain folder gets its own `constants.ts` when it needs one.

Inside each file, group values by feature. Start each group with a `// MARK:` comment so the outline can jump to it. Prefix names so they still read clearly away from the module that uses them (`HAZARD_SPAWN_INTERVAL`, not `interval`).

When a value is shared, it lives in the domain that owns the concept and others import it (`player/` imports `SHIP_CENTER_X` from `../ship/constants`). Do not duplicate it.

`constants.ts` is for tuning, not for every `const`:

- Message schemas stay in `src/networking/messages.ts`
- ECS components stay next to the systems that define them
- Authored data stays in the domain that owns it

```ts
// ❌ BAD — magic number beside the system that uses it
const holdSeconds = 1.5

// ✅ GOOD — src/repair/constants.ts
// MARK: Repair
export const BREACH_REPAIR_HOLD_LEVEL_1_SECONDS = 1.5
```
